# Design: zcode agent adapter

## Problem
Looper speaks two fixed agent protocols (codex exec with
--output-last-message; claude -p with stream-json). The zcode CLI
converges on the Claude Code headless conventions but answers with
a different result contract.

## Approach
Invoke zcode -p with --cwd, --output-format json, and an explicit
permission mode. Parse the one-line summary object, take its
response field, and feed the shared extractor. Planning uses
--mode plan: verified in the zcode source (permission/service.ts)
that plan mode allows read-only tools and denies writes, matching
the codex read-only sandbox role. Workers state --mode yolo
explicitly even though headless defaults to it, so invocation
records show the trust posture.

## Key Trade-offs
- zcode has no structured-output flag: the shape is prompt-borne
  and fenced JSON is tolerated. Weaker than codex/claude flag
  enforcement; this is the known gap the September report flagged.
- No streaming activity interpretation; the dashboard shows the
  log tail, same as codex.
- zcode has no model flag; it uses its own configured model and
  the invocation record stores an empty model.

